
---
import '../styles/global.css';
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="description" content="The October 2026 issue of The Listening Room." />
    <title>October 2026 — The Listening Room</title>

    <style>
      .spotify-embed {
        width: 100%;
        margin: 16px 0;
        overflow: hidden;
        border-radius: 12px;
      }
      .spotify-embed iframe {
        display: block;
        width: 100%;
        max-width: 100%;
        border: 0;
        border-radius: 12px;
      }
      .spotify-embed-placeholder {
        box-sizing: border-box;
        padding: 14px 16px;
        border: 1px dashed var(--line);
        background: var(--paper);
        color: var(--muted);
        font-family: var(--sans);
        font-size: 11px;
        line-height: 1.5;
      }
      .spotify-embed-placeholder p { margin: 4px 0; }
      .spotify-embed-placeholder strong {
        color: var(--burgundy);
        font-size: 9px;
        letter-spacing: .12em;
      }
      .october-favorites-page .spotify-embed { margin-top: auto; }
      .marrow-review-notes .spotify-embed { margin-top: 22px; }
      .hidden-gem-spotify { margin: 12px 0; }

      /* Keep the longer editorial prologue comfortably inside its page. */
      .prologue-page .page-copy {
        box-sizing: border-box;
        padding-bottom: 8px;
      }
      .prologue-page .page-copy h2 {
        font-size: clamp(28px, 3.1vw, 40px);
        line-height: 1.02;
        margin: 0 0 14px;
      }
      .prologue-page .page-copy > p:not(.drop-cap) {
        font-size: 13px;
        line-height: 1.48;
        margin: 0 0 9px;
      }
      .prologue-page .page-copy .drop-cap {
        margin-bottom: 0;
      }

      /* Mobile: let longer magazine pages scroll instead of clipping their content. */
      @media (max-width: 640px) {
        .magazine-viewer {
          width: 100%;
          max-width: 100%;
          padding-left: 10px;
          padding-right: 10px;
          box-sizing: border-box;
        }
        .flipbook-shell {
          width: 100%;
          max-width: 100%;
          overflow: visible;
        }
        #flipbook {
          max-width: 100%;
          margin: 0 auto;
        }
        .flip-page {
          box-sizing: border-box;
          overflow-y: auto !important;
          overflow-x: hidden !important;
          -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch;
          scrollbar-width: thin;
        }
        .flip-page .page-copy,
        .flip-page .playlist-story-copy,
        .flip-page .hidden-gem-copy,
        .flip-page .marrow-review-intro {
          min-height: 0;
          height: auto;
        }
        .flip-page h2 {
          overflow-wrap: anywhere;
        }
        .flip-page p {
          overflow-wrap: break-word;
        }
        .spotify-embed {
          max-width: 100%;
        }
        .spotify-embed iframe {
          max-width: 100%;
        }
        .magazine-controls button {
          min-height: 42px;
          padding: 10px 12px;
        }
      }

      @media (max-height: 700px) {
        .playlist-story-page .spotify-embed { display: none; }
      }
    </style>
  </head>

  <body class="magazine-body">
    <header class="masthead">
      <a class="wordmark" href="/">The Listening Room<span class="period">.</span></a>
      <p class="masthead-note">AN INDEPENDENT MUSIC JOURNAL</p>
    </header>

    <nav class="navigation" aria-label="Main navigation">
      <a href="/">HOME</a>
      <a href="/archive/">THE ARCHIVE</a>
      <a href="/playlists/">PLAYLISTS</a>
      <a href="/album-reviews/">ALBUM REVIEWS</a>
      <a href="/listener-requests/">LISTENER REQUESTS</a>
      <a href="/about/">ABOUT</a>
    </nav>

    <main class="magazine-viewer">
      <div class="magazine-topline">
        <span>THE LISTENING ROOM</span>
        <span>ISSUE NO. 01 · OCTOBER 2026</span>
      </div>

      <div class="flipbook-shell">
        <div id="flipbook">

          <!-- COVER -->
          <article class="flip-page flip-cover">
            <div class="cover-meta">
              <span>ISSUE NO. 01</span>
              <span>OCTOBER 2026</span>
            </div>
            <div class="cover-main">
              <p class="cover-kicker">A QUESTION OF TASTE</p>
              <h1>DO YOUR<br />EARS WORK<span>?</span></h1>
              <p class="cover-author">A PLAYLIST BY ISAIAH WILKINS</p>
            </div>
            <div class="cover-foot">
              <span>THE LISTENING ROOM</span>
              <span>VOL. 01</span>
            </div>
          </article>

          <!-- PAGE 1: PROLOGUE -->
          <article class="flip-page prologue-page">
            <p class="page-label">01 — PROLOGUE</p>
            <div class="page-copy">
              <p class="drop-cap">I</p>
              <h2>A note before<br /><em>you listen.</em></h2>
              <p>I have a habit of hearing things in music that I can't always explain right away. A sound catches my attention. A melody reminds me of something I can't quite place. Two songs that have no obvious reason to sit beside each other suddenly make sense together.</p>
              <p>I've learned not to dismiss those connections just because they're difficult to explain.</p>
              <p>The Listening Room is a place for following them. For sitting with an album a little longer, revisiting a song after the first impression has faded, and paying attention to the details that make music personal. Not every interpretation needs to be universal. Not every favorite needs to be understood by everyone.</p>
              <p>This is the October issue. Inside, you'll find the sounds I've been carrying with me, the records I'm spending time with, and a few things I think deserve a closer listen.</p>
              <p>You don't have to agree with me. In fact, I'd rather you bring your own ears. Just give the music a chance to tell you something you weren't expecting.</p>
              <p>Welcome to The Listening Room.</p>
              <p><em>Isaiah Wilkins · October 2026</em></p>
            </div>
          </article>

          <!-- PAGE 2: CONTENTS -->
          <article class="flip-page">
            <p class="page-label">02 — INSIDE THIS ISSUE</p>
            <h2>In this<br /><em>issue.</em></h2>
            <ol class="contents-list">
              <li><a href="#" data-page="1"><span>Prologue</span><span>01</span></a></li>
              <li><a href="#" data-page="3"><span>Do Your Ears Work?</span><span>03</span></a></li>
              <li><a href="#" data-page="4"><span>Listening Notes</span><span>04</span></a></li>
              <li><a href="#" data-page="5"><span>Album Review</span><span>05</span></a></li>
              <li><a href="#" data-page="7"><span>The Hidden Gem</span><span>07</span></a></li>
              <li><a href="#" data-page="8"><span>Honorable Mentions</span><span>08</span></a></li>
            </ol>
          </article>

          <!-- PAGE 3: FEATURED PLAYLIST -->
          <article class="flip-page playlist-story-page">
  <p class="page-label">03 — THE FEATURED PLAYLIST</p>

  <div class="playlist-artwork-placeholder">
    <span>THE LISTENING ROOM</span>
    <strong>DO YOUR<br />EARS WORK?</strong>
    <small>OCTOBER 2026 · VOL. 01</small>
  </div>

  <div class="playlist-story-copy">
    <p class="eyebrow">8 SONGS · 30 MINUTES, 58 SECONDS</p>
    <h2>A question<br /><em>of taste.</em></h2>
    <p>Sometimes a connection between two songs isn't obvious until you stop hearing them as separate pieces of music.</p>
    <p>“Do Your Ears Work?” follows the threads hiding in production, melodies, and sounds — the things that make songs seem connected even when they don't look like natural companions.</p>
    <p>“I Can't Keep Running” by Chromatics opens the door, leading toward “Man of the Year” by ScHoolboy Q. What interests me isn't just the musical relationship, but how two songs can reach toward a similar ambition and arrive somewhere completely different.</p>
    <p>I don't need every song on a playlist to match. Sometimes the best transition is the one that makes you question why these songs belong together — until you listen a little closer.</p>
    <p>This isn't an invitation to agree with every connection I make. It's an invitation to listen with curiosity. You might hear it immediately. You might not hear it at all. Either way, press play.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="spotify-embed">
    <iframe
